//
// Normative rule hfence-vvma_hfence-gvma_exceptions (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   Attempts to execute HFENCE.VVMA or HFENCE.GVMA when V=1 cause a virtual-instruction exception,
//     while attempts to do the same in U-mode cause an illegal-instruction exception. Attempting to
//     execute HFENCE.GVMA in HS-mode when mstatus.TVM=1 also causes an illegal-instruction
//     exception.
//
// Context:
//   hstatus.HU=1 enables only the hypervisor loads and stores in U-mode, not the fences. With
//     mstatus.TVM=1, HFENCE.GVMA in VS-mode is still HS-qualified (TVM is assumed 0), so it raises
//     virtual-instruction.
//
// Clarifications:
//   HS-qualified (hypervisor.adoc, Virtual Instruction): an instruction is HS-qualified if it would
//     be valid in HS-mode for some register operands, assuming mstatus.TVM=0 and TSR=0.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. VS-mode and VU-mode: HFENCE.VVMA and HFENCE.GVMA with x0/x0 and x6/x8 raise virtual-
//     instruction.
//   2. U-mode with hstatus.HU=0 and HU=1: both raise illegal-instruction.
//   3. mstatus.TVM=1: HFENCE.GVMA raises illegal-instruction in HS-mode and virtual-instruction in
//     VS-mode; HFENCE.VVMA succeeds in HS-mode.
//   All traps: xepc the fence, xtval 0 or its bits, origin the mode.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 3328
//

